    observed: fact("All seven scenarios agree with the hand-written expectation. The first servable decision is period 3, which is the declared lookback, so the warm-up is pinned rather than assumed. Ranking: every one of the 45 decisions whose cross-section holds all four instruments selects (AAPL.NASDAQ, MSFT.NASDAQ) in that order, no other name is ever selected or signalled, the orders are 2500 AAPL and 2631 MSFT filled at 100.00 and 95.00, and the only open positions at the end are AAPL and MSFT. Threshold: the same two names are selected by gt 92, and NVDA and AMZN are never selected and never signalled. Holding period: with the entry at period S = 3 there is no exit at S + 1, there is a flatten at S + 2, and the exit periods are S + 2, S + 4, S + 6 and S + 8, so the cap is counted in decision periods, is reset by the new entry, and never fires part-way through a period. Rebalance schedule: 48 decisions over 12 periods carry the rebalance flag exactly twice, on the first decision of 2022-01-03 and of 2022-01-10, and no LONG signal is submitted on any other decision. Target allocation: the weights are 0.25, 0.25 and 0.16666666666666666 against the pre-cap shares 3/6, 2/6 and 1/6, summing to 0.6666666666666666 within the ceiling, and the strengths are 1.0, 1.0 and 0.6666666666666666, each equal to min(weight / cap, 1.0). No eligible instruments: each of the 48 decisions has an empty selection, no signal, no order, no fill and no position, so the correct behaviour is that nothing happened rather than that the run completed. Opening gap: the entry is read from the platform's own closed position at an average entry price of 100.00, the stop threshold is 90.00, the only exit decision is the first close at or below it, and the fill that follows is 70.00, strictly 20.00 below the threshold, which is the signature of the platform's own fill rather than a fill fabricated at the threshold. The stated tolerances are absolute 1e-12 for a weight or a strength, which carry one decimal-to-float conversion at the Target boundary, absolute 1e-9 for a fill price, which is two-decimal text, and exact for selections, instrument sets, exit tuples, rebalance flags, counts and position quantities, for which a tolerance would hide a difference rather than bound it. One finding is carried rather than a disagreement: the reference strategies' declared full-unit ceiling is not expressible, because portfolio.max_position_weight is bounded to 0.005 through 0.25 by the first-release policy and a payload declaring 1.0 is refused with value_out_of_bound, so the fixture declares the admitted ceiling and hand-computes every weight after the position cap has clamped it, stating both the pre-cap share and the emitted weight", "python/tests/acceptance/discovery_acceptance_bundle.json", 479, "\"observed\": \"All seven scenarios agree with the hand-written expectation. The first servable decision is period 3, which is the declared lookback, so the warm-up is pinned rather than assumed. Ranking: every one of the 45 decisions whose cross-section holds all four instruments selects (AAPL.NASDAQ, MSFT.NASDAQ) in that order, no other name is ever selected or signalled, the orders are 2500 AAPL and 2631 MSFT filled at 100.00 and 95.00, and the only open positions at the end are AAPL and MSFT. Threshold: the same two names are selected by gt 92, and NVDA and AMZN are never selected and never signalled. Holding period: with the entry at period S = 3 there is no exit at S + 1, there is a flatten at S + 2, and the exit periods are S + 2, S + 4, S + 6 and S + 8, so the cap is counted in decision periods, is reset by the new entry, and never fires part-way through a period. Rebalance schedule: 48 decisions over 12 periods carry the rebalance flag exactly twice, on the first decision of 2022-01-03 and of 2022-01-10, and no LONG signal is submitted on any other decision. Target allocation: the weights are 0.25, 0.25 and 0.16666666666666666 against the pre-cap shares 3/6, 2/6 and 1/6, summing to 0.6666666666666666 within the ceiling, and the strengths are 1.0, 1.0 and 0.6666666666666666, each equal to min(weight / cap, 1.0). No eligible instruments: each of the 48 decisions has an empty selection, no signal, no order, no fill and no position, so the correct behaviour is that nothing happened rather than that the run completed. Opening gap: the entry is read from the platform's own closed position at an average entry price of 100.00, the stop threshold is 90.00, the only exit decision is the first close at or below it, and the fill that follows is 70.00, strictly 20.00 below the threshold, which is the signature of the platform's own fill rather than a fill fabricated at the threshold. The stated tolerances are absolute 1e-12 for a weight or a strength, which carry one decimal-to-float conversion at the Target boundary, absolute 1e-9 for a fill price, which is two-decimal text, and exact for selections, instrument sets, exit tuples, rebalance flags, counts and position quantities, for which a tolerance would hide a difference rather than bound it. One finding is carried rather than a disagreement: the reference strategies' declared full-unit ceiling is not expressible, because portfolio.max_position_weight is bounded to 0.005 through 0.25 by the first-release policy and a payload declaring 1.0 is refused with value_out_of_bound, so the fixture declares the admitted ceiling and hand-computes every weight after the position cap has clamped it, stating both the pre-cap share and the emitted weight\","),
