    observed: fact("Every declared rule has a case that fails if the rule is reversed, and the cases are written against the numbers rather than against the implementation: the declared tie rule orders by the feature's value descending and resolves equal values by instrument identifier ascending, a second rule orders by identifier alone, and a rank bound larger than the eligible set takes the eligible set; the position cap clamps without redistributing while the sector cap scales a sector proportionally and an undeclared sector is the instrument itself, and the two caps bind in the declared order; the gross cap scales the already-clamped weights; leave_idle leaves the capped residual uninvested and reallocate redistributes it without exceeding a cap, including the case where no instrument has headroom and the loop must stop; a selection shorter than the portfolio size is not padded and a longer one keeps the ranked leaders; a repeated identifier is weighted once at its first position; a partial fill does not change the next allocation; and an ineligible holding is flattened when the rule says so and left with no target when it does not. An instrument whose feature value was missing produces no row, so it can never be selected - the row contract this fixture pins, which FX-M3-4 then observes for an absent value and FX-M3-1 for a warm-up period. Determinism is asserted by calling the allocation three times over one request that exercises the caps and the reallocating cash policy: the field tuples are identical, the target objects are distinct instances, the request's own held-weight and sector mappings are unchanged afterwards, the emitted targets come back ordered by instrument identifier, each carries its weight and the decision's timestamps, and the same request always produces the same tuple", "python/tests/acceptance/discovery_acceptance_bundle.json", 507, "\"observed\": \"Every declared rule has a case that fails if the rule is reversed, and the cases are written against the numbers rather than against the implementation: the declared tie rule orders by the feature's value descending and resolves equal values by instrument identifier ascending, a second rule orders by identifier alone, and a rank bound larger than the eligible set takes the eligible set; the position cap clamps without redistributing while the sector cap scales a sector proportionally and an undeclared sector is the instrument itself, and the two caps bind in the declared order; the gross cap scales the already-clamped weights; leave_idle leaves the capped residual uninvested and reallocate redistributes it without exceeding a cap, including the case where no instrument has headroom and the loop must stop; a selection shorter than the portfolio size is not padded and a longer one keeps the ranked leaders; a repeated identifier is weighted once at its first position; a partial fill does not change the next allocation; and an ineligible holding is flattened when the rule says so and left with no target when it does not. An instrument whose feature value was missing produces no row, so it can never be selected - the row contract this fixture pins, which FX-M3-4 then observes for an absent value and FX-M3-1 for a warm-up period. Determinism is asserted by calling the allocation three times over one request that exercises the caps and the reallocating cash policy: the field tuples are identical, the target objects are distinct instances, the request's own held-weight and sector mappings are unchanged afterwards, the emitted targets come back ordered by instrument identifier, each carries its weight and the decision's timestamps, and the same request always produces the same tuple\","),
